      "subject": "Scope sheet and route note",
      "shortSummary": "The CIDR scope, jump host, and NAT note for the first scan tasks.",
      "date": "0001-01-01T00:00:00",
      "body": "{player},\n\nUse this scope sheet for the opening tasks:\n\n- Authorized scan CIDR: 10.42.18.0/24\n- Jump host: 10.42.18.10\n- Public portal NAT: https://portal.asterlinktransit.com/status maps to 10.42.18.20\n- ECHO-73 candidate host: 10.42.18.73\n- Out of scope without written expansion: 10.42.30.0/24 and station camera networks\n\nRun netstat -rn on the jump host before you scan. A route table is boring until it prevents a scope mistake.\n\nMira",
      "attachements": []
    }
  ]
}
